THE CASE AGAINST THE TARGET:
The target asserts consensus probability tends to 1 and that reachable matching-cut obstructions are o(1), but it gives no quantitative basin-size estimate. The cut size is monotone decreasing and there are exponentially many absorbing matching cuts: for any perfect matching M whose removal leaves cycles, coloring each cycle monochromatically yields a stable mixed state. Since the dynamics must reduce the cut by Θ(n) edges one flip at a time, the claim that it avoids all such traps with probability 1-o(1) is unsupported; the 'biased walk' on magnetization is not shown to dominate the many local minima on degree-3 graphs, which the target itself calls marginal.

